OL,3,GNEWSACampaigners' 'pride' as court
OL,4,Aoverturns decision to block NI's
OL,5,Alargest road project
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn 2025, a judge ruled against the
OL,8,Fproject going ahead in its current
OL,9,Fform, upholding a legal challenge taken
OL,10,Fby a group of landowners - he said the
OL,11,Fplans breached climate change targets
OL,12,Fand criticised "an inadequacy of
OL,13,Finformation"
OL,15,FNiall McKenna, from the Enough is
OL,16,FEnough campaign which supports the road
OL,17,Fgoing ahead, said it was "not a time a
OL,18,Fcelebration" but said there was "a
OL,19,Fsense of pride"
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/4
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
